message: "If you use TTEOP in your research or product, please cite this work."
title: "TTEOP — Token Telemetry Evaluation Operator Protocol: Specification and Reference Implementation"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "Deric J"
    family-names: "McHenry"
    email: "hello@signalaf.com"
repository-code: "https://github.com/SunrisesIllNeverSee/otep-spec"
url: "https://github.com/SunrisesIllNeverSee/otep-spec/releases/tag/v0.1.3-draft"
abstract: >-
  TTEOP (Token Telemetry Evaluation Operator Protocol) is an open,
  vendor-neutral interoperability standard for measuring AI-operator token
  efficiency. It defines four telemetry primitives (input, output,
  cache_write, cache_read), five derived metrics (Yield, Leverage, Velocity,
  output_fraction, log_leverage), three privacy modes, four provenance
  levels, a JSON Schema for telemetry envelopes, a conformance suite with
  frozen test vectors, and a governance process for protocol evolution.
  The reference implementation is written in JavaScript (Node.js >= 18)
  and published as the npm package tteop-spec.
keywords:
  - token-efficiency
  - ai-operators
  - telemetry
  - protocol
  - open-standard
  - yield
  - leverage
  - cache
  - mcp
  - conformance
